 "text": "Hi, how have you been? The deep freeze is the key. Pack it in there on Friday and it' stay cold for up to a week. Both work, but cubes take up less space. Pack them in layers with lots of air gaps, so they cool evenly. Cover the outside with towels or a blanket to keep the sun off, and put it in a cool, shady spot rather than in the sun. Teach him to close it again straight away. A cool, damp cloth on the lid doesn't hurt either. Yes, let it sit overnight so the ice melts slowly. Pour it out in the morning and refreeze.",
